 "commands": [
  "bun tools/compile-rivals.mjs --runs 2 --sizes 1000,4000 --apps 2000 --twins hashmap,bintrees,strings,json,dyncall,iterchain,ecs",
  "syn1000 and syn4000 are flat 20-unit projects; app2000 is a 3-layer 20-unit dependency DAG (4 foundation + 8 domain + 8 service modules/packages/crates/TUs) using generics, interfaces/traits, Option/optional, and hash maps, edited in mid-layer unit mid4",
  "Grail's store before each cold run: grail cache warm (every standard module); Go's GOCACHE holds its standard library, Zig's cache its compiler_rt, and cargo uses the offline registry, so the standard library is warm for every toolchain",
  "one process: GRAIL_JOBS=1, GOMAXPROCS=1 GOFLAGS=-p=1, make -j1, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1; four jobs: the same at 4",
  "Grail: check `grail check`, build `grail build` (grail.toml project with 20 modules under src/)",
  "C/C++: multi-TU Makefile (`clang -O0 -g -fuse-ld=lld`, `clang++ -std=c++20 -O0 -g -fuse-ld=lld`); check runs `-fsyntax-only` per changed TU",
  "Go: check `go vet ./...`, build `go build -o syn .` (20 packages under module `syn`)",
  "Zig: check `zig build-exe -fno-emit-bin main.zig`, build `zig build-exe -O Debug -fno-llvm -fno-lld main.zig` (self-hosted x86_64 backend, 20 imported modules)",
  "Rust: check `cargo check --offline -q`, build `cargo build --offline -q` (20-crate Cargo workspace)",
  "edit: one constant in one function body inside module m10 changes; a twin gets one statement added to main"
 ],
